notes.body:
Right, you can wrap files_identical in a local static function that has the appropriate signature.

To deal with the order, the paths that have already been visited can be kept in a hash table, but instead of putting all of them into a hash table and then iterating a second time, you would append to the string at the moment of inserting into the hash table. `g_hash_table_add` returns TRUE if something is not already in the hash table, so a loop like

```c
if (g_hash_table_add(unique_paths, new_path)) {
   g_string_append_printf(path_str, ...);
}
```

should work.

